# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the two values from Supabase.
# Both are safe to expose (anon key is meant to be public — RLS protects your data).
# See SETUP.md step 2b.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...replace-me...

# Optional: base URL of the Python RAG service (see rag/README.md). When set, the
# Fitness Guru tab grounds answers for Pro users in the curated KB + their history
# via pgvector (the service checks Pro server-side). Leave unset to use the direct
# Gemini path.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_RAG_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Optional: RevenueCat PUBLIC SDK keys that power ComeBack Pro subscriptions.
# Get them at app.revenuecat.com → Project → API keys (the "public" app keys).
# Leave unset to keep billing off (Pro features stay locked). See docs/MONETIZATION.md.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=appl_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=goog_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional, DEV BUILDS ONLY: force the client's Pro flag on so the Life Coach can be
# demoed without a sandbox purchase. Inert in production builds (__DEV__ is false and
# NODE_ENV is "production"); never unlocks server-side Pro. See lib/demo.ts.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEMO_PRO=1

# Optional, DEV BUILDS ONLY: run with an in-memory set of sample rows and a local demo
# user instead of Supabase (no network, nothing persists). Every screen shows an amber
# DEMO DATA badge; the Intimacy tab's demo PIN is 1234. Same production guards as above.
# See lib/demo.ts and lib/demo-data.ts.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEMO_DATA=1
